# NOTE=GBP-VIDEO-001 PHYSICALLY EXECUTED 2026-09-16, one run, no Game Pak: the 003A sequence, then ONE install of the 003B extended one-shot and 209 admitted cycles of the repeated drained service (CHECK_ADMISSION -> record reset -> unmask -> ISR -> READ -> AUDIO -> VIDEO -> ACK pending|0x8000 -> PI clean -> IRQ:=0 -> WAIT_NEXT). Result ok_video_sequence_capture, capture=target_reached at 88 VIDEO blocks, restore ok, errors 0, uncertain 0. 209 unmasks / 209 ISR entries / 209 ACK / 209 re-arms / 0 reentry / 0 main W1C / 1 teardown W1C. Sources: 121 x 0x0400, 65 x 0x0100, 23 x 0x0500 -> 144 AUDIO and 88 VIDEO drains, 0 timeouts, 0 busy, 0 unexpected.
# NOTE=the 232 "B" lines are the physical whole-block reads (88 VIDEO 0xF00 at 0x01100000, 144 AUDIO 0x1000 at 0x01800000). Their bytes are NOT in this script: the VIDEO bytes and NINE of the AUDIO blocks live in the sequence sidecar above. Only the first 8 successful AUDIO drains and the last valid one preserve a payload by design; the other 135 AUDIO drains have metadata (address, length, rc, timing) but NO recorded bytes and NO CRC. A "B" line carries a CRC-32 only when the payload was actually measured: 88 of 88 VIDEO lines and 9 of 144 AUDIO lines. A blank CRC field means "not measured", never "the CRC is zero". The replay reports the 135 unbacked AUDIO reads as missing blocks instead of inventing bytes.
# NOTE=frame-start boundaries recomputed from raw_first4: GBI and the Start-up Disc agree on every one of the 88 blocks (0 divergences), both giving positions 0, 25, 65 and intervals 25, 40. ONE complete boundary-to-boundary interval of exactly 40 VIDEO blocks was observed (seq25 -> seq65, 680138 ticks = 16.79353 ms = 59.547 Hz in this run). The first interval of 25 is a startup transient, NOT a 25-block frame: the four VERIFY cycles at the start cost 34792 ticks each against 3101 for a lean cycle, and the device VIDEO block is single-buffered, so roughly twelve blocks were produced while the probe was still servicing and were never signalled as separate causes.
# NOTE=payload: under both references' byte 1 / byte 3 picking the 88 blocks carry exactly TWO semantic payloads - 85 blocks of 960 x 0x7FFF and 3 blocks (seq 0, 25, 65, the frame starts) of 0xFFFF followed by 959 x 0x7FFF. The complete frame seq25..seq64 is an all-white frame with the start marker on its first element. Byte 0 differs from byte 1 in 688 of 84480 words, always ff/7f, never at offset 0 of a 32-byte DMA line, and byte 2 never differs from byte 3; the byte1/byte3 payload of seq0 is byte-identical to the GBP-AV-SERVICE-001 physical block although the raw CRCs differ (fe45ff08 vs ef18fc8d), and both give GBI checksum 0x7F0FFF10.
# NOTE=INTSR polling loops replay with one time-base read per sample, so poll counters differ from the device run; every other value is the console's. The handler's own PI reads and its single W1C live inside each "I u" record and are not replayed operations. The 210th cause was latched after the last re-arm, refused at the admission point (target reached) and closed by the teardown's single W1C - it was never delivered, so no 210th "I u" exists.
